As a club officer interested in running for USG Senate next year, the knowledge base doesn’t yet include the 2027 election timeline or candidate filing instructions.

Based on the latest available Elections page, last updated June 1, 2026, USG Senate elections are handled through the USG Elections process, and candidates were required to complete steps like:

- submitting candidate materials for publication, including a statement, platform, questionnaire responses, and preliminary finance plan;
- getting preliminary finance plans approved before purchasing campaign items;
- emailing campaign social media handles to **usgelect@usc.edu**;
- following campaign-period deadlines posted on the USG Elections website.

For next year, your best move is to contact the Elections team directly at **usgelect@usc.edu** and monitor the USG Elections page when the next cycle opens.

Also, as context: the Senate consists of **twelve elected Senators** representing USC undergraduates, and Senators work with students and student organizations on campus projects and advocacy. If you want to learn more about the role before running, you can contact the Speaker of the Senate at **usgsots@usc.edu**.

